diff --git a/docs/lane-a-foundation/README.md b/docs/lane-a-foundation/README.md
index 0708fa074..118244f4a 100644
--- a/docs/lane-a-foundation/README.md
+++ b/docs/lane-a-foundation/README.md
@@ -58,3 +58,21 @@ distributed anti-rollback, durable operations, durable AuthBus policy/quota, or
 any external effect not proven by an exact-candidate receipt. Remaining
 implementation and external gates are listed in
 [`REMAINING_GATES.md`](REMAINING_GATES.md).
+
+
+### Multiple protocol surfaces within one module
+
+The protocol registry retains exactly one top-level row per module in the fixed
+Lane A order. A row may contain `additionalProtocols`, a one-level list of full
+protocol records owned by that same module. Readers that resolve current protocol
+IDs must enumerate both the primary record and these additions; a flat-only
+reader remains a primary-surface reader and must not claim complete coverage.
+Current and legacy IDs are globally unique, source paths must exist, and nested
+additions/unknown record fields fail validation. No wire protocol or authority
+semantics are changed by this navigation representation.
+
+For kernel.operations, durable-ledger-outbox.v1 and its reference-model legacy ID
+retain the standalone/reference lineage. The complete durable-owner.v1 addition
+retains the CognitiveStore product-owner sources and invariants. The separate
+CAPABILITY_EVIDENCE_V2 file remains standalone source evidence; canonical Lane A
+capability receipt counts come only from CAPABILITY_EVIDENCE_MAP.json.
